WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.600
Missing security requirements leave teams without clear expectations for authentication,

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:10.340
authorization, auditing, data protection, rate limits, approval workflows,

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.240
or CUI handling.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:17.100
Threat modeling helps teams identify likely abuse paths before code is deployed.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:21.640
It is most useful when it covers trust boundaries, sensitive data flows,

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.420
privileged actions, and failure modes.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:29.680
Unsafe business logic can allow attackers to bypass intended workflows even when

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:32.140
individual endpoints operate as written.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:37.080
Sequence enforcement, approval checks, and state validation are design concerns.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.460
Architecture reviews help identify misplaced trust in internal networks,

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:46.000
client-side controls, service integrations, or manual processes.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:50.460
CMMC-aligned systems need defensible decisions and traceable risk handling.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:53.720
Use threat modeling for critical workflows and trust boundaries.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:58.020
Integrate secure SDLC practices into design and development.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.960
Perform security architecture reviews for systems that handle or affect CUI.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:10.700
Selected CMMC mappings for this topic include RA.L2-3.11.1 - Risk assessments;

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:15.800
CA.L2-3.12.1 - Security assessments.
